            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 85-year-old male patient, admitted on 12/09/1990 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Blood tests were performed to exclude infectious or other contributing causes. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. Physiotherapy for airway clearance was initiated. The patient was discharged in stable condition with optimised inhaler therapy. We recommend close follow-up and continued pulmonary rehabilitation in the outpatient setting. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you have any questions.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
